completed_at: "2026-08-16T06:16:11.990Z"
author: "harness:codex"
estimated_minutes: 300
acceptance_criteria: "Parse every documented docs --add form through one SDK-owned linked-resource primitive; preserve URI schemes byte-for-byte; turn Markdown and CSV label/path pairs into exactly one typed entry; reject malformed or ambiguous pairs before mutation; keep files/docs CLI and PmClient behavior aligned; cover unit, integration, packed-consumer, negative-control, and help-contract paths; document the supported grammar and token-efficient recovery."
goal: project management = context management
objective: Make document evidence links lossless and unambiguous across SDK and CLI mutation paths.
value: "Agents can attach PRs, issues, and runbooks without silently destroying the context they are recording."
impact: Corrupted evidence links make item history look complete while the primary source is unreachable.
outcome: One SDK parser owns linked-resource pair syntax and all CLI/package adapters preserve exact URL identity.
why_now: GitHub #1038 reproduces both advertised pair syntaxes returning success with wrong persisted data.
parent: pm-usfg
risk: high
confidence: high
severity: high
environment: pm docs linked-resource mutation on 2026.8.15
repro_steps: "Add a bare URL, Markdown link pair, CSV label/path pair, and path=/note= pair; compare the stored row count, path bytes, and note."
resolution: Linked documentation parsing preserves Markdown and CSV URL references as one remote doc with its label retained as context.
expected_result: Each documented labeled form yields one entry whose path is the original URL and whose note is the label; ambiguous input is refused without mutation.
actual_result: "Markdown input is stored literally with https:// collapsed to https:/, while CSV input is split into two rows."
